# =========================================================
# RANK 1 - "Doorway"
# GATE: char son_2, rank 1, period afternoon, room kitchen
# =========================================================

~ start

$> locals.tone = 0
$> GameState.location("Kitchen · Afternoon")
$> GameState.sprite("son_2", "doorway")

The back door bangs. Then boots. Then he's in the frame.

Tyler: [#mood=neutral, #pose=doorway] Practice got out early.

Mom: [#mood=neutral, #pose=standing] Mm.

He doesn't come in. He stands where the frame cuts him in half.

Tyler: [#mood=neutral] Coach made us run the hill. Six times.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] Good.

Tyler: [#mood=neutral] It's not good. It's stupid. It's October.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] It's October.

Tyler: [#mood=surprised] ...Point is, six.

She keeps her eyes down. The pan needs turning and the pan is a good excuse.

Tyler: [#mood=neutral] I'm not even tired.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] You're dripping on the floor.

Tyler: [#mood=soft] I'll mop it.

He doesn't move. He's waiting.

- Look up.
	$> locals.tone += 1
	She looks up. He's flushed and pleased and pretending not to be.
	Tyler: [#mood=flushed] What.
	Mom: [#mood=neutral] Nothing. You wanted me to look.
	Tyler: [#mood=flushed] I didn't say that.
	Mom: [#mood=soft] You didn't have to.
- Keep not looking.
	Mom: [#mood=neutral] Mop it, then.
	Tyler: [#mood=strain] ...Yeah.
	He gets the mop out. He's loud about it. He wants her to hear the effort.
- Ask about the six.
	Mom: [#mood=neutral] Six times up the hill.
	Tyler: [#mood=surprised] You were listening.
	Mom: [#mood=neutral] I was in the room.

He mops. The floor is already clean where he's mopping.

Tyler: [#mood=neutral] Coach says I could go regional.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] Coach says a lot of things.

Tyler: [#mood=strain] He means it though.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] Mm.

He stops. The mop handle is between both hands and he's holding it too hard.

Tyler: [#mood=averted] You didn't say anything. About regional.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] Regional's good.

Tyler: [#mood=averted] Right.

He puts the mop away. He takes a while about it.

Tyler: [#mood=neutral] I'm gonna be outside.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] Mm.

He's at the door.

Then he stops there, one hand on the frame.

Tyler: [#mood=averted] You could come out. Watch. If you wanted.

He doesn't wait for the answer.

$> GameState.apply("tyler_r1", locals.tone)

$> GameState.rank_card("son_2", 1)

=> END
